/* Isolation probe, and the one that costs: an extra predicate argument that is
   never read but ALTERNATES between 0 and 1.  Constant-argument erasure cannot
   remove it -- it is not constant -- so it survives into the well-founded
   template as a third coordinate, and the qualifier generator emits
   combinations over pairs and triples of coordinates: 27 qualifiers here
   against 10 for the pass-through twin, for one extra variable that no
   certificate can use.  Measured at 51 s against 0.6 s for the twin.

   What this isolates: the cost is not the extra argument (the twin has one and
   is free), not an extra predicate (`..._twopred_noflag_valid.hes` adds one and
   is free), and not the real sort (this file is entirely integer).  It is an
   argument whose value changes.  An analysis that removed arguments that are
   never READ, rather than only those that are CONSTANT, would erase `d` here. */
Main 0
s.t.
Main (z:int): bool =mu forall (a:int). forall (b:int). (a = 0 /\ b = 0) \/ Q a b 0;
Q (a:int) (b:int) (d:int): bool =mu a > 0 /\ b >= 0 \/ Q (-b) a (1 - d);
